    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0623" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2231/391: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-11T16:00:00-04:00">May 11, 1939—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Your despatch 470, May 5.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d576-f1"/> Notice given by
                    Foreign Minister does not indicate what schedule products it is desired to
                    restrict, extent of restriction in each case, or share of each global quota
                    intended to be allotted to the United States.</p>
                <pb facs="0624" n="616" xml:id="pg616"/>
                <p>You should secure specific proposals from Tobar on above questions and transmit
                    substance thereof by telegram, keeping in mind provisions of second paragraph of
                    Article VII regarding 30 day period within which agreement should be
                    reached.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d576-f1" n="26" xml:id="d576-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see telegram No. 31, May 5, 4 p.m., <hi rendition="#italic"
